Package: pdfrune
Title: Ultra-Fast, Memory-Safe, Permissive PDF Engine
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Gwang-Jin", "Kim", email = "gwang.jin.kim.phd@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Gwang-Jin Kim [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Gwang-Jin Kim <gwang.jin.kim.phd@gmail.com>
Description: Clean-room, high-performance, memory-safe, and permissively-licensed
    PDF engine written in Rust with R bindings. Provides fast text, word, block,
    layout, and table extraction, rasterization to 'RGBA' pixel buffers and vector SVG,
    document creation and manipulation, outlines (table of contents), hyperlinks,
    image extraction and insertion, annotations, true content-stream redactions,
    interactive 'AcroForm' widgets, multi-threaded batch processing, and ISO 32000
    standard encryption. Built strictly against open ISO 32000 specifications
    under MIT or Apache-2.0 licenses with zero 'AGPL' restrictions.
License: MIT + file LICENSE | Apache License 2.0
URL: https://github.com/gwangjinkim/pdfrune
BugReports: https://github.com/gwangjinkim/pdfrune/issues
Depends:
    R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports:
    jsonlite
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc
Encoding: UTF-8
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
